# __TITLE__

Interactive full-precision inference for **__TITLE__**, one of the BYOD
(Build Your Own DLM) models. It uses the exact `__SOURCE_CHECKPOINT__` LoRA checkpoint
from the corresponding experiment and loads its original base model in BF16.
No 4-bit quantization is used.

Generation starts from masked answer positions and refines them in parallel.
Fewer denoising steps than generated tokens provide a sub-autoregressive
inference budget; increasing the step count gives the model more refinement
opportunities.

The interface includes PMI bigram Viterbi, confidence-guided and random
retention, autoregressive confidence, block diffusion, early stopping,
EOS/EOT retention delay, and plain-text output for copying newlines and code.

Viterbi defaults to temperature 2, top-k/candidates 16,
fixed bigram weight 0.5, PMI minimum count 1, clipping ±2, and diffusion
probability for retention confidence. Ending-delay strength is set to 10.
The checkpoint and evaluation controls are hidden to keep the interface simple;
these defaults can be edited in `app.py`. The sparse scorer uses the complete 980,000-response
training split, separately tokenized for this model. The scoring and retention
defaults can be edited near the top of `app.py`.

Model: [__MODEL_REPO_ID__](https://huggingface.co/__MODEL_REPO_ID__)

This is a research demo. Outputs may be inaccurate or inappropriate and
inherit limitations from the original base model.
